{"kind":"report","text":"Approved G3's first typed/window Source at exact candidate 2a80a300f8df3ca444d290694467c648dc1e5366, tree 885562284ab53b1f77d619537279831a4311f393. Primary fd4fdb0b read FIRST IN FULL, then all 24 changed paths. This complete review answers 49f191c4 under implementation 011a539f/promise 3e8fee0e and planner's first-head decision 72c9d5e5. No changes requested. Durable presence is explicitly a later second head.\n\nConclusion 1: the implementation meets that bounded contract. Three typed carousels route operator alerts, present tender work and head-grower watering requests. The generic for rule is admitted under restricted@1 and binds only to a complete many source. Related reads bind to existing entry-definition projections at the installation root, with no caller scope/item selectors or explicit-item source. The production viewer comes from native session claims checked against the signer key and membership, plus current membership standing; the display handle is not identity. Native projection authorization, ownership and limits remain in force.\n\nThe Grow task rule distinguishes covered present, covered absent and unavailable evidence. A wrong-room leave does not cancel presence in the current room; another member or membership incarnation does not establish this member's location. Taken work remains with its native performer. Missing coverage produces an unavailable item placeholder with native identity and exact read points, without its unassigned body, actor, acts or raw source rows; it does not become an empty queue. Complete native data remains server-held for admission, and the app receives only the routed card and queue metadata. Separate primary and root read heads are exposed honestly, without an atomic cross-scope snapshot claim. Immediately before signing, the interpreter rereads current routing and related evidence; false or unknown refuses even at an unchanged task revision. Explicit record-by-id reads bypass routing and retain ordinary native grant/state admission.\n\nThe generic app retains empty Back and refresh, recovers a shortened queue to position zero only for automatic refresh, refuses out-of-range explicit navigation and stale cuts, and retains a captured unknown original/check through routing changes. Constant controls are available on routed summaries; required Report text uses the existing exact scalar tool. The old native definitions and projection objects remain unchanged; the source JSON is 62,680 bytes within its existing bound. Documentation matches these limits and behaviors.\n\nConclusion 2: the tests are meaningful at their stated boundaries. Native grow-routing.test.ts covers actual Core/SQLite Site comments and two actual Room births, exact signer/room/entry facts, window eviction and replay. Its queue witness proves all nine operator/day/head selections, another-room tender, explicit records, leaving and coverage loss at unchanged task revision before any signature, covered negative and wrong-room leave, competing Take, owner Report, lost decision grant, Approve/Decline and consistent replay. The production installed-Worker witness in scope/grow-owned-scopes.test.ts separately invokes the native-session viewer, current grants and both related Site reads on empty queues, preserving the existing SDK grid/layers and replay assertions. It does not claim production nonempty routing. Generic declaration/interpreter tests cover rejected forms/foreign related reads and viewer identity, nonboolean/error placeholders, changed routing, shortened refresh and unknown-original retention. Existing G2 test edits preserve assertions while accounting for optional app-facing data.\n\nThe one adverse control removes only the current unknown-route admission refusal, replacing it with a comment. Independently compared the frozen source snapshots: original equals current source exactly, and no second guard changes. The unchanged native queue witness passes, fails by one signature versus zero after evidence eviction, then passes after exact restoration; all three log hashes match. This distinguishes pre-sign refusal from a later business refusal. No sweep.\n\nMy independent run of the unchanged browser witness passes 320 and 592 pixels, each resized live to the other width and back. Cached Playwright 1.63.0, Chromium 153.0.8010.12, Node 26.12.0; Browser plugin unavailable, authorized isolated loopback fallback, public TEST actors. The actual kit/Core/SQLite/MCP custody flow has unavailable body suppression and read-point retry, arrival recovery, quiet unchanged refresh, app-only model denial, Take and scripted text Report, operator Hold, watering Approve/Decline, empty Back and later-request polling, exactly five native MCP signatures per width and consistent Site/Room replay. No horizontal overflow or app/console errors. Visually inspected the narrow unavailable/read-points card and desktop task/Take card; wrapped native identifiers and controls are readable without clipping. Capture-only outer height expansion is restored before interaction.\n\nIndependently ran the two focused routing files unchanged: 2 files, 8 cases pass. My additional pure rule probe uses the actual task expression with eleven hand-chosen evidence sequences, including wrong-room leave, move then old-room leave, leave then return, other-member evidence and foreign membership incarnation. Extra checks cover taken-by-other, wrong Room incarnation and missing grant. All pass. These hand-written projection rows are explicitly a pure rule boundary, not native authority evidence.\n\nBoth generated resources independently match their builds: MCP generated.ts 154,693 bytes, SHA256 735c9069ffea9b5462da05371b6b96d5b9dddf5df5953f7cd023a42cbc11267b; Page assets.ts 825,119 bytes, SHA256 4ed36958254123c284d6a714ab287b1d35779d1a1f61026e63a202b153b0a767, unchanged from G2. The MCP browser graph has 50 inputs, no Wrangler/unenv input and no external imports.\n\nConclusion 3: validation cost and remaining limits are explicit. Original full gate at clean fdb9b467d06b47a3d7ff67753a516ab726b05ef8/tree36c149316412ad31ad622289c89a9f0882000ce0 passed, checkpoint 092be4e9, original PTY 83240 closed exit 0. Raw logs show 399 files/1926 cases pass, 1 file/3 cases skipped, Node 31 and Counting 55 pass; whitespace and typecheck pass. Only the evidence note differs afterward. Outer 490.33 seconds elapsed/701.97 seconds CPU (604.88 user + 97.09 sys); typecheck 8.19/31.56 and test 481.90/670.18. Warm shared macOS 27.0.1 arm64, 18 CPUs, Node 26.12.0, initial load 2.11/1.73/1.71, all known builder test/compiler/browser processes closed at start, zero installs. No exclusive CPU, physical heap, provider usage or total edit-cost claim. Raw cancellation, scripted reset/SQL and Content-Type warnings remain separate stability work. I did not repeat the full gate or whole suite.\n\nThe initial phone browser timeout remains a failed development observation without an exact frozen input manifest. It exposed lost polling after an empty result; the current generic refresh fix and independent later-request browser flow distinguish the correction. Earlier fixture admission, literal/reference and receipt-versus-refreshed-card failures remain qualified historical failures. The final gated browser manifest's 33 hashes were independently verified against the exact passing commit; it is not conflated with the initial failure.\n\nIndependently materialized all 2287 Git mode/blob leaves: 2263 unchanged from audited Main 4b4d58b0 and exactly the 24 named changed paths. Both artifact queries are exhausted, 37/37 and 7/7 total live bases, with 20/4 exact candidate bindings fresh; native prepare confirms primary-first assigned implementation binding. Stable-copied all 497 finite-map leaves/8,855,652 bytes under map SHA256 07c2597d546acabea8ef07d9054a288646f8317cccfae186a007a2a933b5827b. All 226 historical snapshots match their named Git commits. Exact listed dependency manifests show 106 lock-matching versions; four nested vendor/variant manifests are not independent lock entries. All frozen original leaves, isolated copies, map and candidate leaves reread unchanged at completion. No adjacent private dependency traversal, installation, owner driver/sealer execution, source/ref mutation, push or deployment.\n\nChecker scratch /private/tmp/checker-g3-routing-qjpezvri contains validation.json, review-validation.json, owner-evidence-validation.json, dependency-metadata-validation.json, generated-validation.json, independent-probe.json, focused.log, browser.log and browser/report.json/proofs/captures. Nonempty Grow installation, membership/session and grant lookup remain explicit TEST ports; the report is a scripted consumer, not an external LLM transcript. Native issued-session production behavior is separately bounded by the empty-queue owning witness. No production nonempty routing, device execution, hosting/provider, persistent presence, P1 or S2 completion is claimed. Landing still requires the actual native receipt and audit.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fd4fdb0bec922fc801477c97e7aedd4f013f9395","binding":"assigned","head":"2a80a300f8df3ca444d290694467c648dc1e5366","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:940818cc2309ddd1140878d94d0bdab900e5ef20\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3e8fee0e8cf5d340f3672808988c7b2791a666c5\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:940818cc2309ddd1140878d94d0bdab900e5ef20","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}